          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %strong ind-object
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is a
            %strong
              formal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimit
            of objects of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+presheaves"} category of presheaves
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            (the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            is written
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ind
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ind
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C})
          %p
            Here, “ind” is short for “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+system"}> inductive system
            ”, as in the inductive systems used to define
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+colimits"} directed colimits
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pro-object"} pro-object
            corresponding to “projective system”.
          %p
            Recalling the nature of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi c
                    %mn 4
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  c_1 \hookrightarrow c_2 \hookrightarrow c_3 \hookrightarrow c_4 \hookrightarrow \cdots
          %p
            of objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            are regarded to converge to an object in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            itself. Standard examples where ind-objects are relevant are categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            whose objects are finite in some sense, such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+sets"} finite sets
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite dimensional vector spaces
          %p
            Moreover, ind-categories allow one to handle “big things in terms of small things” also in another important sense: many
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large categories
            are actually (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalent
            to) ind-categories of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small categories
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
            (see the description of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C})
            in terms of that of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            below). Such
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/large+category"} large categories
            equivalent to ind-categories are therefore called
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+category"} accessible categories
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p There are several equivalent ways to define ind-objects.
          %h3#as_diagrams As diagrams
          %p
            One definition is to define the objects of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ind
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ind
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            to be diagrams
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:D\to \mathcal{C}
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered
            category.
            %br>/
            The idea is to think of these diagrams as being the placeholder for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            over them (possibly non-existent in
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
            with the corresponding diagram
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1\to \mathcal{C}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:D\to \mathcal{C}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mi E
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G:E\to \mathcal{C}
          %ol
            %li
              The embedding
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo →
                      %mi ind
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}\to ind
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              should be
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful
            %li
              each diagram
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi D
                    %mo →
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:D\to \mathcal{C}
              should be the colimit of itself (considered as a diagram in
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ind
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ind
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              via the above embedding), and
            %li
              the objects of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              should be
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact
              in
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ind
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ind
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
          %p Thus, we should have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi ind
                          %mtext -
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mo ,
                          %mi G
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mi ind
                          %mtext -
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mi F
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi e
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi E
                          %mi G
                          %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                          %msub
                            %mi lim
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi ind
                          %mtext -
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi e
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi E
                          %mi G
                          %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                          %msub
                            %mi lim
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi e
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi E
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi ind
                          %mtext -
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %mi G
                          %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                          %msub
                            %mi lim
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi e
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi E
                          %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                          %mi 𝒞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi F
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %mi G
                          %mi e
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  ind\text{-}\mathcal{C}(F,G) &amp;= ind\text{-}\mathcal{C}(colim_{d\in D} F d, colim_{e\in E} G   e)\\
                  \&amp;\cong lim_{d\in D}\; ind\text{-}\mathcal{C}(F d, colim_{e\in E} G e)\\
                  \&amp;\cong lim_{d\in D} colim_{e\in E}\; ind\text{-}\mathcal{C}C(F d, G e)\\
                  \&amp;\cong lim_{d\in D} colim_{e\in E}\; \mathcal{C}(F d, G e)
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p Here
          %ul
            %li
              %p the first step is by assumption that each object is a suitable colimit;
            %li
              %p
                the second by the fact that the contravariant Hom sends colimits to limits (see properties of
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            %li
              %p
                the third by the assumption that each object is a
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/compact+object"} compact object
            %li
              %p
                the last by the assumption that the embedding is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
          %p
            So then one
            %em defines
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ind
                  %mtext -
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi E
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  ind\text{-}\mathcal{C}(F,G) \coloneqq lim_{d\in D} colim_{e\in E}\; \mathcal{C}(F d, G e)
                  \\,.
          %h3#as_filtered_colimits_of_representable_presheaves As filtered colimits of representable presheaves
          %p
            Recall the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/co-Yoneda+lemma"} co-Yoneda lemma
            that every presheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in PSh(\mathcal{C})
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            over
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable presheaves
          %p
            there is a functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : D \to \mathcal{C}
            (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            possibly large) such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  X \simeq colim_{d \in D} Y(\alpha(d))
          %p
            (with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C}) \subset PSh(\mathcal{C})
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(\mathcal{C}) = [\mathcal{C}^{op},Set]
              on those
              = succeed "/" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functors"} functors
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaves"} presheaves
              which are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+colimit"} small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representables
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi colim
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi D
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \simeq colim_{d \in D} Y(\alpha(d))
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              some
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
            %p
              Those for which
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              may be chosen to be
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℕ
                        %mo ≤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}^{\leq}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sequential+colimits"} sequential colimits
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+ind-objects"} strict ind-objects
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{op}\to Set
              belonging to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C})
              under this definition — those which are small filtered colimits of representables — have an equivalent characterization as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flat+functor"} flat
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+presheaf"} small
              functors
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi 𝒞
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{op}\to Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{op}
              had them”. In particular, if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              has finite colimits, then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C})
              consists exactly of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+exact+functor"} left exact
              small functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}^{op}\to Set
              (see proposition 
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IndRepresentableIffFlat"}>
              ).
            %p
              For more equivalent characterizations see at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a{:href => "accessible+category#definition"} accessible category – Definition
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              Given that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathcal{C}^{op},Set]
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C})
              defined in this way is its “free cocompletion under filtered colimits.”
          %p
            To compare with the first definition, notice that indeed the formula for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-sets"} hom-sets
            is reproduced:
          %p Generally we have
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Set
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Y
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Set
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mi Y
                          %mi F
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                              %mo ′
                          %mi Y
                          %mi G
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≃
                          %msub
                            %mi lim
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mi 𝒞
                            %mi op
                          %mo ,
                          %mi Set
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi Y
                          %mi F
                          %mi d
                          %mo ,
                          %msub
                            %mi colim
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mo ′
                              %mo ∈
                              %mi D
                              %mo ′
                          %mi Y
                          %mi G
                          %mi d
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  [\mathcal{C}^{op},Set](X,Y)
                  \&amp; \simeq
                  [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set](colim_{d \in D} Y F d, colim_{d' \in D'} Y G d)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; \simeq
                  lim_{d \in D} [\mathcal{C}^{op}, Set]( Y F d, colim_{d' \in D'} Y G d)
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            by the fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-functor"} hom-functor
            sends
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limits"} limits
            in its first argument (see
            %em properties
            at
            = succeed ")." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
          %p
            By the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            this is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                      %mo ′
                  %mi Y
                  %mi G
                  %mi d
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq
                  lim_{d \in D} (colim_{d' \in D'} Y G d')(F d)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Using that
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(\mathcal{C})
            are computed objectwise (see again
            %em properties
            at
            = succeed ")" do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mi lim
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                  %msub
                    %mi colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi D
                      %mo ′
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi F
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mi d
                  %mo ′
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots \simeq
                  lim_{d \in D} colim_{d' \in D'}
                  \\mathcal{C}(F d, G d')  \,.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Let
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FinDimVect"} FinDimVect
                be the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite-dimensional+vector+spaces"} finite-dimensional vector spaces
                (over some
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                be an infinite-dimensional vector space. Then
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                can be regarded as an object of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ind
                      %mo −
                      %mi FinDimVect
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ind-FinDimVect
                as the colimit
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi colim
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                          %mo ′
                          %mo ↪
                          %mi V
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim_{V' \hookrightarrow V} Y(V')
                over the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+category"} filtered category
                whose objects are inclusions
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ↪
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V' \hookrightarrow V
                of finite dimensional vector spaces
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V'
                into
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                of the representables
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi V
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %msup
                        %mi FinDimVect
                        %mi op
                      %mo →
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y(V') : FinDimVect^{op} \to Set
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
                is the
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                the category of finitely presented objects of some equationally defined structure,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ind
                      %mtext -
                      %mi 𝒞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ind\text{-}\mathcal{C}
                is the category of all these structures.
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    The category
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grp"} Grp
                    of
                    = succeed "s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
                  %ul
                    %li
                      The category
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ab"} Ab
                      of
                      = succeed "s" do
                        %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
                %li
                  %p
                    The category
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
                    of
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sets"} sets
                    is the ind-category of the category of
                    = succeed "." do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+indexed+sets"} finitely indexed sets
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+scheme"} formal scheme
                is an ind-object in
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            In the following we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}^f
            for the “formal colimits” defining ind-objects. I.e. if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi ℐ
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝒞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha \colon \mathcal{I} \to \mathcal{C}
            is a small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagram"} diagram
            and with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Ind
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi PSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Ind(\mathcal{C}) \hookrightarrow PSh(\mathcal{C})
            the defining inclusion, then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %munder
                      %mi lim
                      %mo ⟶
                    %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo ≔
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %munder
                    %mi lim
                    %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}^f (\alpha)
                  \\;\coloneqq\;
                  \\underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim} (i \circ \alpha )
                  \\,.
          %h3#the_category_of_indobjects The category of ind-objects
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              then so is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Ind
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝒞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C})
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C})
              admits small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
              and the defining inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ind
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ind(\mathcal{C}) \hookrightarrow PSh(\mathcal{C})
              commutes with these colimits.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#KashiwaraSchapira06"} KashiwaraSchapira 06, theorem 6.1.8
          %p
            The following says that morphisms between ind-objects are represented by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+transformation"} natural transformation
